    "vision_reason": "This is a woven/embroidered baby-carrier sling with cross-motif embroidery and geometric bands, a form typical of Southeast Asian highland or archipelago textile traditions used for carrying infants; the style (cross-stitch-like X motifs, red/black/white geometric bands) is more consistent with an upland or eastern Indonesian/mainland Southeast Asian group than classic Javanese batik-and-applique work described, but as a textile object plausibly used in the region it fits the broad \"made/used by the people\" criterion given no contradicting evidence of a distant unrelated culture.",
